From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 12:22:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/25] Cross-check Patala 2 against VedaVishtaram directly (no
 external prompt)

Done by hand the same way Patala 10-11 were previously, at the lead's
request. Two real findings:

1. The "82 vs 41/42 sutra" count gap noted at ingestion time is a chapter-
   scope difference, not a numbering bug: VedaVishtaram's own Patala 2
   page content stops at sutra 42; its Patala 3 is the accent chapter,
   confirmed by its own opening sutras, not a continuation of Layer A's
   43-82. Those 40 sutras have no VedaVishtaram counterpart at all and
   remain uncross-checked by this source.

2. Within 1-42, resolved 5 previously-uncertain sutras with real evidence,
   via a new P2_RESOLUTIONS table (kept separate from P10_11_RESOLUTIONS
   so its scope stays honest): 2.8/2.27 via the recurring "purva" pattern
   (2.27 by a direct VedaVishtaram match the automated same-index matcher
   had missed, because VedaVishtaram's sandhi-joined rendering doesn't
   have the word-boundary space the matcher's anchor assumed); 2.33 via
   one direct match plus the standard technical term "purva-rupa"; 2.36
   via a genuinely new resolution kind -- VedaVishtaram's own page
   corrupts an avagraha into a literal zero-width-non-joiner character,
   confirmed at two separate sutras (2.24 and 2.36), not a missing letter.
   2.40 was checked and left honestly unresolved: VedaVishtaram's own
   excerpt for that sutra doesn't reach the position in question.

Also found and fixed a real, pre-existing bug: crosscheck_vedavishtaram.py
unconditionally appended to the corpus's "note" field, so a second run
duplicated the whole cross-check sentence. Now dedupes on re-run.

The RV 1.1.7 visarga-before-aa gap this was meant to help resolve remains
open -- VedaVishtaram carries no Bhasya at all for sutras 2.24/2.27's
region, so the text is now confirmed clean but the interpretive question
isn't settled. A promising new lead surfaced instead for the separate Q2
(word+iti sandhi) question: sutra 2.51, sitting in the uncovered 43-82
block, which cannot be confidently parsed without a commentary this
corpus doesn't have -- flagged, not acted on.

Four new tests in tests/test_rv_pratishakhya_import.py cover the new
resolutions and the verified-range boundary. Architecture doc sec.6.10
and PENDING.md record the full trail.

